{"_fixture_note":"Assembled from the REST pull_request object GitHub returned for a pull request at the head of a real force-push (before cdab69df, after 2d726c4f); not a captured webhook delivery; the author login is replaced by a neutral one. Replace it with a real synchronize capture during the R5b-2b live walk.","action":"synchronize","number":139,"before":"cdab69dfb2ebddbff5e70315f676e6e75301ddb7","after":"2d726c4fcc4f522d9a480a295bd09b50e684f3ca","pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/pulls/139","id":4805477569,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU9XKPM8AAAABHm3EwQ","html_url":"https://github.com/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/pull/139","diff_url":"https://github.com/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/pull/139.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/pull/139.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/issues/139","number":139,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add the runner_verified execution mode, closed to the route","user":{"login":"acme-owner","id":124836611,"node_id":"U_kgDOB3DbAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124836611?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner","html_url":"https://github.com/acme-owner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acme-owner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds the third execution mode, `runner_verified`, so a repository can hold it and a verified run can be claimed, issued and finished. The mode stays closed: the route that sets a repository's mode still refuses it (400 `mode_not_available`, existing test untouched), so no real repository can enter it until the later opt-in change. The pg tests set the mode on the row directly.\n\nWhat changes:\n- Migration 0771 widens `repos_execution_mode_check`. It also widens, with unchanged bodies and only the mode predicate touched, the database filters that mean \"a run on a runner\": the job write, the queue lister, the no-job lister, the notice lister (and its row policy), and the mode-switch cancel, its audit function and its row policy. The cancel function now refuses a repo that is still on either runner mode; the audit function refuses a cancelled-run count on any move that stays on a runner.\n- `@fx/runner` gets one list of runner modes (`RUNNER_MODES`, `isRunnerMode`, plus a SQL list built from the same constant). The registry now has three keys; `runner_verified` is a runner target whose job mode is `verified`. Every reviewer role is refused there with the new closed reason `verified_review_not_wired`, before anything is dispatched (they move to our sandbox in a later PR).\n- Claim takes a pending run of either runner mode whose repo is currently on a runner mode. The issuer writes `verified` exactly when the run's own mode is `runner_verified`. `done` accepts both modes and the run keeps its own mode. The queue sweep backstop and the mode-switch cancel act only when the repo's new mode is not a runner mode, so a move between the two runner modes cancels nothing.\n- The staging cloud-to-proxy pin is added to `PINNED_GIT_PROXIES` as a hash pair; production stays unpinned. No host text is in the build (a test scans for it).\n\nSite-by-site: which sites mean \"on a runner\" (now `isRunnerMode`) and which mean \"local-only\" (literal kept).\nOn a runner: claim query (`runnerClaims`), job issuer mode, `done` route, queue sweep, notice sweep, follow-up dispatch (uses the child's own mode), the recorded pull request lookup (`advance.ts`, `githubReads`), role card choice (`seat`), executor prompt runtime and the Spec file-list refusal (`build`), the Spec-pin check in `runStatusWriter`, the job-write and listers in SQL.\nKept as `runner_local`: the GitHub fence (`localOnlyHttp`, the fenced branches of `mergeGateRun` and `advanceReviewSteps`, the `local` option of the recorded-PR lookup), `RUNNER_ADMIN_OK_SQL`, the local-review opt-in, the preview refusal, sandbox allowances, and the approval definers (a verified repo's approval path belongs to the change that opens the mode).\n\nExisting tests that asserted \"verified is closed\" at the repo or registry level were changed to the new state. The tests that guard a migration by running a cluster without it (0754, 0757, 0759) now also leave 0771 out of that \"before\" cluster, since 0771 replaces functions those files create.\n\nMutation checks, run for real: (a) making the issuer always write `\"local\"` turns the \"signed job says verified\" test red; (b) making the queue sweep's backstop use `!== \"runner_local\"` turns the \"verified run on a verified or runner_local repo is not cancelled\" test red. Both were reverted.\n\nFix round: the route's own cancel branch is now reached by pg cases that put a fixture repo on `runner_verified` and call the route. A move to `runner_local` cancels nothing (the verified run stays pending, audit row says 0 cancelled, old mode `runner_verified`); a move to `sandbox` cancels the pending verified and local runs with `execution_mode_changed` and the audit row records `from: runner_verified`. Mutation (b), on that exact line: reverting `isRunnerMode(old) && !isRunnerMode(new)` to `=== \"runner_local\"` turned the move-to-sandbox test red; restored, green. The allowance set-aside is noted in code as staying `runner_local`-only.\n\nNot faked: nothing new on the network. The staging proxy pin is only exercised live in the later walk.\n\nSize and reading notes: the diff is about 650 lines against a 500-line target; 261 of them are the migration, which has to restate full SQL function bodies to change one predicate, and the size was accepted. For a reviewer role in a verified repo, \"no row is written\" is read as: the run ends as a `refused_spend` row with `verified_review_not_wired` and no job is issued, like every other admit refusal (changing that would mean changing `startAgentRun` for all modes). The staging pin is tested by the committed hash pair, the true/false logic on synthetic origins, and a scan that `keyring.ts` holds no host text.\n\nGate 1: pending\nGate 2: pending\n\nRefs D#6\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01NAVAYFp6qnpgbRcLnrUqr3\n","created_at":"2026-10-09T20:24:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T21:15:03Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"10f414728e47022251579be9726aac2fa5e46cae","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12563303768,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU9XKPM8AAAAC7NTNWA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/labels/code-review-needs-fix","name":"code-review-needs-fix","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"Code review found issues \u2014 needs fixes","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12563304096,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU9XKPM8AAAAC7NTOoA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/labels/security-review-passed","name":"security-review-passed","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Security review passed","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/pulls/139/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fulcrumaxe/fulcrumaxe-cloud/pulls/139/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fulcrumaxe/